---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title='Marcelo Ojeda | Software Architect · Integration · SaaS';
const description='Software Architect with 20+ years designing, integrating and evolving critical systems, enterprise platforms and SaaS products.';
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} lang="en">
<section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Software Architecture · Santiago, Chile</p><h1>Complex systems.<br/><span>Clear decisions.</span></h1><p class="lead">I design, integrate and evolve platforms that support real operations — from enterprise ecosystems and omnichannel retail to SaaS products built from the ground up.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#work">View architecture stories</a><a class="button" href="/en/about/">Professional profile</a></div><div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><strong>20+ years</strong><span>engineering, architecture and integration</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>50+ stores</strong><span>retail ecosystem and omnichannel operations</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>0 → SaaS</strong><span>multi-tenant B2B product from inception</span></div></div></section>
<section id="work"><p class="eyebrow">Architecture Stories</p><h2>Problem first.<br/>Technology second.</h2><p class="kicker">Cases explained through context, constraints and decisions — with enough depth to understand both business impact and the architecture behind it.</p><div class="cards"><a class="card" href="/en/architecture/retail-omnichannel/"><span class="num">01 · RETAIL / INTEGRATION</span><h3>From B2B operations to an omnichannel ecosystem</h3><p>Stores, e-commerce, marketplaces, ERP, WMS, inventory and logistics evolving as one connected system.</p><span class="arrow">↗</span></a><a class="card" href="/en/architecture/saas-platform/"><span class="num">02 · SaaS / PRODUCT</span><h3>A multi-tenant B2B product from scratch</h3><p>Domain, security, APIs, frontend, persistence and cloud designed as a coherent product.</p><span class="arrow">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section><p class="eyebrow">How I work</p><h2>Architecture that reaches production.</h2><div class="process"><div><b>01</b><h3>Context</h3><p>Business, constraints, legacy systems and operational risk.</p></div><div><b>02</b><h3>Decisions</h3><p>Explicit boundaries, integrations and trade-offs.</p></div><div><b>03</b><h3>Execution</h3><p>Technical depth to validate the design.</p></div><div><b>04</b><h3>Evolution</h3><p>Systems designed to change without being rebuilt.</p></div></div></section>
<section><p class="eyebrow">Technical depth</p><h2>An architect who stays close to code.</h2><p class="lead">Java, Spring Boot, REST APIs, React, SQL and Google Cloud are tools. The focus is designing boundaries, integrating systems, reducing complexity and making technology serve the business.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Software Architecture</span><span class="tag">Solution Architecture</span><span class="tag">Systems Integration</span><span class="tag">SaaS</span><span class="tag">Java / Spring Boot</span><span class="tag">REST APIs</span><span class="tag">GCP</span></div></section>
<style>h1 span{background:linear-gradient(90deg,#f3f7fb 10%,#73a7ff 55%,#a78bfa);-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent}.cards .card:first-child{transform:translateY(1.5rem)}.cards .card:first-child:hover{transform:translateY(calc(1.5rem - 6px))}@media(max-width:760px){.cards .card:first-child{transform:none}}</style></BaseLayout>